The taxi stops in front of the building.
I take my big bag.
It is very heavy.
There is an elderly watchman at the gate.
He looks at me.
"Madam, who are you?" he asks.
"Are you new here?"
I smile.
"Yes, I am the new resident," I say.
"My name is Maya."
He smiles warmly.
"Welcome, Maya madam," he says.
He comes near my bag.
"Is the bag heavy?" he asks.
"Yes, it is very heavy," I say.
He lifts my bag.
He shows me the stairs.
"The stairs are there," he says.
I go inside with him.
